    "description": "An integer, or ``int`` is a number of the set \u2124 = ``{..., -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, ...}``. It is limited by ``PHP_INT_MIN``, the lower bound, and ``PHP_INT_MAX``, the upper bound. \n\nIntegers have several syntaxes: they may be written in binary, octal, decimal, hexadecimal and with ``_`` as a separator.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    $a = 1234;       // decimal number\n    $a = 0123;       // octal number (equivalent to 83 decimal)\n    $a = 0o123;      // octal number (as of PHP 8.1.0)\n    $a = 0x1A;       // hexadecimal number (equivalent to 26 decimal)\n    $a = 0b11111111; // binary number (equivalent to 255 decimal)\n    $a = 1_234_567;  // decimal number (as of PHP 7.4.0)\n\n?>",
